{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "prbs-auth-collection-2026",
    "name": "PRBS Auth API",
    "description": "End-to-end tests for the AuthController on prbs-backend (Phase 5).\n\n## Setup\n\n1. Start the backend:\n   ```bash\n   cd prbs-backend\n   export JAVA_HOME=\"$(/usr/libexec/java_home -v 17)\"\n   mvn spring-boot:run\n   ```\n2. Start Mailpit (so OTPs are auto-captured from the email):\n   ```bash\n   brew install mailpit && mailpit\n   ```\n3. Import this collection. The pre-filled collection variables already point at `localhost:8080` and `localhost:8025`.\n4. Run the **Happy Path** folder top-to-bottom — tokens and the 6-digit OTP code are captured into collection variables automatically.\n\n## What's covered\n\n- Feature 1 (OTP generation) — Send OTP\n- Feature 2 (email delivery) — verified via Mailpit auto-extract\n- Feature 3 (JWT issuance + refresh) — Verify OTP, Refresh, Logout\n- Negative paths — wrong code, unknown email, inactive user, validation errors\n- Rate limit (use Collection Runner with iterations ≥ 11)\n\n## What's NOT covered here\n\n- Feature 4 (role-based protection) — needs an authenticated endpoint. Add `MeController` and use the `Extensions / GET /me` request.\n- Features 5 + 6 (reminder, booking confirmation) — need `BookingDevController` with the `dev` profile active. See the Extensions folder.\n\nSee the README in this folder for the controllers to add.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Happy Path",
      "description": "Run these requests top-to-bottom. Tokens + OTP code flow between them automatically.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Send OTP (Alice — student)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('returns 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "",
                  "// Auto-capture OTP from Mailpit so the next request doesn't need manual copy/paste.",
                  "// Silently no-ops if Mailpit isn't running — just set the `otp` variable by hand.",
                  "const mailpit = pm.collectionVariables.get('mailpitUrl');",
                  "pm.sendRequest(`${mailpit}/api/v1/messages?limit=1`, (err, res) => {",
                  "  if (err || !res || res.code !== 200) {",
                  "    console.log('[postman] Mailpit not reachable; set the `otp` variable manually.');",
                  "    return;",
                  "  }",
                  "  const msgs = res.json().messages;",
                  "  if (!msgs || msgs.length === 0) return;",
                  "  pm.sendRequest(`${mailpit}/api/v1/message/${msgs[0].ID}`, (err2, res2) => {",
                  "    if (err2 || !res2 || res2.code !== 200) return;",
                  "    const body = (res2.json().HTML || '');",
                  "    const m = body.match(/>(\\d{6})</);",
                  "    if (m) {",
                  "      pm.collectionVariables.set('otp', m[1]);",
                  "      console.log('[postman] Captured OTP:', m[1]);",
                  "    }",
                  "  });",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\"\n}" },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/send-otp",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "send-otp"]
            },
            "description": "Triggers `OtpService.generateAndPersist` (feature 1) and `EmailService.sendOtp` (feature 2). The 6-digit code lands in Mailpit; the test script reads it and stores it as `{{otp}}`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Verify OTP",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('returns 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('has accessToken', () => pm.expect(body.accessToken).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);",
                  "pm.test('has refreshToken', () => pm.expect(body.refreshToken).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);",
                  "pm.test('user role is STUDENT', () => pm.expect(body.user.role).to.eql('STUDENT'));",
                  "",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', body.accessToken);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', body.refreshToken);",
                  "console.log('[postman] Tokens captured.');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"code\": \"{{otp}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/verify-otp",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "verify-otp"]
            },
            "description": "Issues `AuthResponse{accessToken, refreshToken, user}` (feature 3). Tokens are captured into `{{accessToken}}` and `{{refreshToken}}`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Refresh access token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('returns 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('access token rotated', () => pm.expect(body.accessToken).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', body.accessToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/refresh",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "refresh"]
            },
            "description": "Re-issues an access token. The refresh token itself isn't rotated (feature 3, refresh middleware)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "4. Logout",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('returns 204', () => pm.response.to.have.status(204));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/logout",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "logout"]
            },
            "description": "Revokes the refresh-token JTI in the in-memory store."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "5. Refresh after logout (must fail)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('returns 401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                  "pm.test('error code is TOKEN_INVALID', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('TOKEN_INVALID'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/refresh",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "refresh"]
            },
            "description": "Proves the revocation store actually invalidates the JTI (feature 3, revocation)."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Negative cases",
      "description": "Validate error envelopes — {code, message} JSON per the GlobalExceptionHandler.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Send OTP — unknown email → 404",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('returns 404', () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));",
                  "pm.test('code is USER_NOT_FOUND', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('USER_NOT_FOUND'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"nobody@nowhere.example\"\n}" },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/send-otp",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "send-otp"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Send OTP — inactive user → 403",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('returns 403', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));",
                  "pm.test('code is USER_INACTIVE', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('USER_INACTIVE'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"chidi@university.ac.rw\"\n}" },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/send-otp",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "send-otp"]
            },
            "description": "Chidi is seeded with status=INACTIVE in V6__seed_demo_users.sql."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Verify OTP — wrong code → 401",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('returns 401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                  "pm.test('code is OTP_INVALID', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('OTP_INVALID'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"code\": \"000000\"\n}" },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/verify-otp",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "verify-otp"]
            },
            "description": "Run after a Send OTP. Wrong codes increment the token's `attempts`; 5 failures lock the token."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Verify OTP — non-numeric code → 400 validation",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('returns 400', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('code is VALIDATION_FAILED', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('VALIDATION_FAILED'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"code\": \"abcdef\"\n}" },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/verify-otp",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "verify-otp"]
            },
            "description": "VerifyOtpRequest's `@Pattern(\\d{6})` rejects this at the controller boundary."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Send OTP — missing email → 400 validation",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('returns 400', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{}" },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/send-otp",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "send-otp"]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Rate limit",
      "description": "Open Collection Runner, select just this folder, set Iterations ≥ 11. The 11th request returns 429.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Send OTP (rapid-fire)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.info.iteration < 10) {",
                  "  pm.test('200 within limit', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "} else {",
                  "  pm.test('429 over limit', () => pm.response.to.have.status(429));",
                  "  pm.test('Retry-After=60', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Retry-After')).to.eql('60'));",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\"\n}" },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/send-otp",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "send-otp"]
            },
            "description": "RateLimitFilter caps each IP at 10/min on /api/v1/auth/**."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Extensions (require code additions)",
      "description": "These requests prove features 4, 5, 6 — but they need a small amount of code added to prbs-backend first. See the README in this folder.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /me — feature 4 (role-based protection)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('returns 200 with bearer token', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "me"]
            },
            "description": "Requires `MeController`. Returning UserSummary for the authenticated user proves the JWT auth filter populates the SecurityContext."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /me — no token → 401",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('returns 401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "me"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /_dev/bookings — features 5 + 6",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('returns 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('reminderSent starts false', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().reminderSent).to.eql(false));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"studentId\": 1,\n  \"supervisorId\": 7,\n  \"name\": \"Alice Uwase\",\n  \"groupNumber\": 3,\n  \"project\": \"AI Crop Disease Monitor\",\n  \"slotAt\": \"2026-05-20T13:30:00\",\n  \"meetUrl\": \"https://meet.google.com/abc-defg-hij\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/_dev/bookings",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "_dev", "bookings"]
            },
            "description": "Requires `BookingDevController` (@Profile(\"dev\")) and the backend started with --spring.profiles.active=dev.\n\nAfter this returns 200, check Mailpit: you should see TWO new emails — Booking Confirmed (to alice) + Session scheduled (to supervisor). That's feature 6.\n\nFor feature 5 (reminder), set `slotAt` to NOW + 2 minutes, then wait. The reminder scheduler fires once a minute; within ~2 minutes a third email lands in Mailpit and `reminder_sent` flips to true in the DB."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Backend root."
    },
    {
      "key": "mailpitUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8025",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Mailpit web UI + REST API for auto-capturing the OTP. Leave empty to disable auto-capture."
    },
    {
      "key": "email",
      "value": "alice@university.ac.rw",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Seeded student. Other seeded options: supervisor@university.ac.rw, admin@university.ac.rw, chidi@university.ac.rw (INACTIVE)."
    },
    { "key": "otp",          "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "accessToken",  "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "refreshToken", "value": "", "type": "string" }
  ]
}
